# ABAP Delivery Preferences (always-on)

Apply together with `abap-project-conventions`. These preferences come from
real session friction (company laptop, no GitHub, SE38 paste workflow).

## Delivery format

- Prefer **pasteable ABAP in chat** (method / class section). Do not rely on
  GitHub URLs or VM paths (`/opt/cursor/...`) as the only delivery channel.
- If output may truncate: say so, then continue from the next line when the
  user says `계속` — without re-pasting completed parts.
- When adding controls/members: always ship **DEFINITION + IMPLEMENTATION**
  together (e.g. `mo_stats_dlg` / `mo_stats_html` / `on_stats_close` with
  `show_stats`). Never give a method body that references undeclared members.

## Before open-ended UX work

- If the request is vague (“있어보이게”, “멋지게”, “데모용”) **and** no brief
  is attached: run skill `abap-requirement-intake` **once** (≤8 choices), then
  build to `abap-ops-monitor-ux`.
- If `docs/templates/ops-monitor-request-brief.md` is filled/pasted: skip
  questions; state Build Contract; implement.

## Quality defaults (when user does not specify)

- Popups (STATS/HELP/KPI): HTML dialogbox, not plain `MESSAGE`.
- Charts needing color/orientation: HTML/CSS viewer, not IGS-only.
- ALV toolbar: Find / Sort / Filter only unless asked otherwise.
- Read-only invariants never relaxed without an explicit exception.

## Language

- User-facing UI copy and intake questions: Korean.
- Match surrounding file language for docs/commits.
